09:33:35 said  You now have a working desktop version of the photo editor with the original's preset strip: square tiles showing your own photo with each look applied, white caption bars that turn blue when selected, and thin lines between groups. It also has the sliders, film and effects tools, masks, crop, colour tables, saving your own presets and export, and it passes every Craft Anything check.
09:33:35 said  In this last round I read the original's code and fixed two things. The preset panel now uses the original's real sizing rule, 20% of the window height, and the colour steps run in the original's order, with colour tables after the sliders, which changes how every look comes out.
09:33:35 said  The preset names and colour tables are my own recreations, not the originals, so the looks are similar in style but won't match exactly, and the slider strengths are my estimates. Some of the original's rarer tools, such as Super 8 and tone curves, aren't included. I also never saw the original running, because no picture of that screen exists in its files, so the panel is built from the code's measurements and hasn't been compared with the real thing.
09:33:36 said  If you can, send a phone screenshot of the original's preset screen and ask me to match anything that looks different.
